<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hieronymus von Colloredo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1732">1732</a>–<a href="/years/1812">1812</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hieronymus von Colloredo was the last ruling prince-archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a>, elected in 1772. An enlightened reformer, he is best remembered as the employer of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfgang-amadeus-mozart">Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart</a>, who left his service in 1781. He fled before French troops in 1800, and the archbishopric was secularised in 1803.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hieronymus-von-colloredo.jpg" alt="Hieronymus von Colloredo" width="320" height="469" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann M. Greiter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hieronymus_Graf_von_Colloredo_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
